        "size":  2839,
        "content":  "================================================================\nUNSC RESOURCE GUIDE: SHIPPING \u0026 SUPPLY CHAIN STATISTICS\n================================================================\n\nUse these statistics in the Security Council to quantify the impact of geopolitical conflicts on global trade.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n1. RED SEA \u0026 SUEZ CANAL DISRUPTIONS (2023-2024)\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• Suez Canal Transit Drop: Daily transit volume through the Suez Canal dropped by over 45% following Houthi attacks in the Bab-el-Mandeb.\n• Transit Cost Spikes: Rerouting container ships around the Cape of Good Hope (Africa) adds 10-14 days to journey times and increases fuel costs by over $1 million per round trip.\n• Global Container Rates: Spot freight rates from Shanghai to Europe increased by over 250% between December 2023 and February 2024.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n2. STRAIT OF HORMUZ ENERGY FLOWS\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• Oil Volume: Approximately 20.5 million barrels of oil per day pass through the Strait of Hormuz (representing 20% of global petroleum consumption).\n• LNG Shipments: Over 20% of global liquefied natural gas (LNG) shipments transit through Hormuz, primarily sourced from Qatar.\n• Choke Point Dependency: Over 75% of crude oil transiting Hormuz is destined for Asian markets (China, India, Japan, South Korea).\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n3. THE RUSSIAN SHADOW FLEET\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• Tanker Count: Estimates indicate the Russian shadow fleet consists of over 600 aging tankers (many older than 15 years, nearing decommissioning).\n• Insurance Deficit: Over 90% of these vessels operate without verified Protection and Indemnity (P\u0026I) insurance from major Western clubs.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n4. SEMICONDUCTOR \u0026 RAW MATERIAL CONCENTRATIONS\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• Advanced Chips: Over 90% of the world\u0027s most advanced semiconductors (under 10nm) are manufactured in Taiwan, highlighting the supply chain risk of regional conflict.\n• Rare Earth Elements: China processes over 85% of global rare earth elements, critical for electric vehicles and defense systems.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• UNCTAD Maritime Transport Review\n• International Energy Agency (IEA) Energy Statistics\n• World Bank Food Security and Trade Bulletins\n• Lloyd\u0027s List Intelligence Reports\n================================================================\n"
