        "content":  "================================================================\nUNSC RESOURCE GUIDE: USEFUL SOURCES \u0026 TRADE WATCHDOGS\n================================================================\n\nThis document lists the most reliable organizations and databases to monitor for real-time shipping and trade data during committee.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n1. INTERGOVERNMENTAL MARITIME BODIES\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• International Maritime Organization (IMO):\n  - Website: https://www.imo.org\n  - Focus: The specialized UN agency responsible for the safety and security of shipping and prevention of marine pollution.\n• UN Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD):\n  - Website: https://unctad.org\n  - Focus: Publishes the annual Review of Maritime Transport, the definitive statistical analysis on global fleet sizes, container volumes, and transit costs.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n2. TRADE \u0026 ECONOMIC WATCHDOGS\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• World Trade Organization (WTO):\n  - Website: https://www.wto.org\n  - Focus: Tracks global trade disputes, tariff changes, and trade restrictive measures under national security exceptions.\n• World Bank Group - Global Trade Portal:\n  - Website: https://www.worldbank.org\n  - Focus: Tracks food security indices, fertilizer supply chains, and infrastructure development loans.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n3. INDUSTRY INTELLIGENCE \u0026 RESEARCH ORGS\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• Lloyd\u0027s List Intelligence:\n  - Website: https://lloydslistintelligence.com\n  - Focus: Provides real-time tracking of merchant shipping, vessel registrations, insurance status, and port delays.\n• ICC International Maritime Bureau (IMB):\n  - Website: https://www.icc-ccs.org/icc/imb\n  - Focus: Tracks global piracy incidents and acts of armed robbery against ships in real-time.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nOFFICIAL SOURCES\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n• United Nations General Assembly Maritime Affairs Database\n• International Energy Agency (IEA) Oil Market Reports\n================================================================\n"
